⍝ Migration step 2: export every component to JSON lines, in export/.
⍝ Run:  dyalog sample-scripts/component-files/export-json.apls
⍝ One line per component:  {"file":"orders","component":3,"value":{…}}
⍝ Also writes export/checks.json: counts and totals computed here in APL,
⍝ so the loader can check the database got exactly the same data.
here←⊃1⎕NPARTS⊃2⎕NQ'.' 'GetCommandLineArgs'
dir←here,'data/' ⋄ out←here,'export/'
{}3 ⎕MKDIR out
J←{1(⎕JSON⍠'HighRank' 'Split')⍵}               ⍝ matrices → lists of rows
(names types)←0 1(⎕NINFO⍠1)dir,'*.dcf'
:For f :In names[⍋names]
    name←2⊃⎕NPARTS f
    t←f ⎕FTIE 0
    (first next)←2↑⎕FSIZE t
    lines←{
        o←⎕NS''
        o.(file component)←name ⍵
        o.value←⎕FREAD t ⍵
        J o
    }¨first+¯1+⍳next-first
    (⊂lines)⎕NPUT(out,name,'.jsonl')1
    ⎕FUNTIE t
    ⎕←'export/',name,'.jsonl: ',(⍕≢lines),' components'
:EndFor

⍝ Checks: what the database should contain afterwards
t←(dir,'customers')⎕FTIE 0 ⋄ cust←⎕FREAD¨t,¨2+⍳¯3+2⊃⎕FSIZE t ⋄ ⎕FUNTIE t
t←(dir,'orders')⎕FTIE 0 ⋄ ord←⎕FREAD¨t,¨⍳¯1+2⊃⎕FSIZE t ⋄ ⎕FUNTIE t
c←⎕NS''
c.customers←≢cust
c.credit_total←+/4⊃¨cust
c.orders←≢ord
c.order_lines←+/≢¨ord.lines
c.order_value←(⌊0.5+100×+/{+/×/⍵[;2 3]}¨ord.lines)÷100
(⊂J c)⎕NPUT(out,'checks.json')1
⎕←'export/checks.json: ',J c
